 C# Append Text to File Example
Description

This program demonstrates how to append (add) new text to an existing text file using StreamWriter and File.AppendText() in C#.

Source Code
csharp
// Append

StreamWriter writer = File.AppendText("c##.text");

writer.WriteLine("jamal");
writer.WriteLine("jamal");

writer.Close();

Explanation
StreamWriter writer;
Declares a StreamWriter variable used to write text into a file.
File.AppendText("c##.text");
Opens the existing text file and allows new text to be added at the end of the file.
writer.WriteLine("jamal");
Adds the word "jamal" to the file on a new line.
writer.WriteLine("jamal");
Adds the word "jamal" again on another new line.
writer.Close();
Closes the file after writing.
Output

The text file will contain the previous content plus the new lines:

text
shukri cabdullahi mohamud
zada cabdullahi moxamud
jamal
jamal
Important Note
File.AppendText() adds new text at the end of an existing file without deleting its previous content.

If the file does not exist, it creates a new file.
Conclusion
StreamWriter is used to write text into a file.
File.AppendText() adds new content to the end of a file.
WriteLine() writes text on a new line.
Close() closes the file after writing.

