C# Open and Read a Text File
Description
This program demonstrates how to open a text file using OpenFileDialog, read its contents using StreamReader, and display the information in a ListBox.
StreamReader reads;
DialogResult result;
result = openFileDialog1.ShowDialog();
// Check user selection
if (result == DialogResult.OK)
{
    reads = File.OpenText("c##.text");

    string lines;
    while (reads.EndOfStream == false)
    {
        lines = reads.ReadLine();
        listBox1.Items.Add(lines);
    } reads.Close();
}
Explanation
StreamReader reads;
Declares a StreamReader variable used to read data from a text file.
DialogResult result;
Declares a variable to store the user's selection.
openFileDialog1.ShowDialog();
Opens the Open File Dialog window so the user can select a file.
if (result == DialogResult.OK)
Checks whether the user selects a file and clicks Open.
File.OpenText("c##.text");
Opens the specified text file for reading.
string lines;
Declares a string variable to store each line read from the file.
while (reads.EndOfStream == false)
Checks whether the file has reached its end. The loop continues while there is more text to read.
reads.ReadLine();
Reads one line of text from the file.
listBox1.Items.Add(lines);
Displays each line inside the ListBox.
reads.Close();
Closes the file after reading all its contents.
Output
The contents of the selected text file will appear inside listBox1, one line at a time.
Example:
text=ca242,jmahuriya universty,c# progaraming
There is one improvement needed in the original code.
reads = File.OpenText("c##.text");
reads = File.OpenText(openFileDialog1.FileName);
This allows the program to open the actual file selected by the user.
reads.Close();
After the while loop.//Conclusion
StreamReader reads text from a file.
OpenFileDialog allows the user to select a file.
DialogResult.OK confirms the file selection.
File.OpenText() opens a text file.
ReadLine() reads one line at a time.
EndOfStream checks whether the file has ended.
Items.Add() displays text in a ListBox.
Close() closes the file.

